# Local secrets for developer tools. Copy this file to `.env.local` (gitignored) and fill it in:
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# `yarn dev` needs none of this: the game and admin panel run with no env at all. Nothing loads
# this file automatically. Tools that need it load it themselves, e.g.
# `node --env-file=.env.local scripts/generate-audio.ts`.
#
# Never put a key here that starts with NEXT_PUBLIC_: Next.js puts those in the browser bundle.
# Never put secrets in apps/server/data/settings.json: admin settings are data, not secrets.
# Server deployment settings (ADMIN_TOKEN, WEB_ORIGIN, MCP_ACCESS, …) go in deploy/.env on the VPS;
# see deploy/.env.example.

# ── ElevenLabs (audio generation) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used only on your machine, by the script that generates music, sound effects and bot voice
# lines into apps/web/public/audio/. Players never call ElevenLabs, so production needs no key.
#
# Getting a key:
#   1. Sign in at https://elevenlabs.io → Developers → API Keys → Create API Key.
#   2. Give it access only to what the script needs: Text to Speech, Sound Effects, Music and
#      Voices (Voice Design). Leave everything else off.
#   3. Set a credit limit on the key so a script bug cannot spend your whole plan.
#   4. Paste it below. If it ever leaks, delete it in the dashboard and create a new one.
#
# Licensing: audio from the free plan is non-commercial and needs attribution. Generate the
# assets you ship on a paid plan, and check the current terms for Eleven Music.
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
